## Your Task
Address the critic findings. For each gap and each "absent_unjustified" checklist/taxonomy result:
- **Either** add the missing element(s) to the RevisionDelta
- **Or** dismiss it with a one-sentence justification in its gap disposition
- When adding or correcting feedback authority, distinguish values the source
  legitimately sets from values the system must establish independently. Cite
  `Use case: ...` or an exact target-evidence `ref`, and state the scope in
  domain words rather than restating the source kind.

Focus on real behavioral deficiencies. Dismiss findings that duplicate existing coverage or target capabilities the system does not have.

## Gap dispositions
Each gap above starts with its gap ID (`G-1`, `G-2`, ...). Give exactly one
entry in `gap_dispositions` for each gap ID, with these fields:
- `gap_id`: the gap ID exactly as shown above.
- `disposition`: `addressed` when this reply adds or changes elements for the
  gap; `dismissed` when you judge the gap a false positive or already covered;
  `recommendation` when the gap is a requirement-backed safeguard that the
  supplied sources do not establish as a current function, kept as a proposed
  design recommendation rather than added to the structure.
- `element_ids`: for `addressed`, the IDs of the elements this reply adds or
  changes for the gap, as written in this reply (responsibility, constraint,
  process-model part, control action, feedback channel, controlled process,
  coordination link, or mechanism IDs). For `dismissed` or `recommendation`,
  the IDs of existing elements the justification relies on, or `[]`.
- `justification`: one sentence saying what the change does for the gap, why
  the gap is dismissed, or what the recommendation proposes.

A `dismissed` or `recommendation` disposition is only for a gap this reply
leaves unchanged. An `addressed` gap must appear as added or modified elements
whose IDs its `element_ids` list: in `new_responsibilities`,
`new_controlled_processes`, `new_coordination_links`, or
`modified_responsibilities`. Describing a change in the justification does not
make it; to change an existing responsibility, even one feedback channel or
variable, restate that responsibility in `modified_responsibilities`.
